-- title:
--   Components of the glued resolution are pulled back chart labels
-- statement:
--   Fix $N_0$ nonzero and a prime $q$ with $q \nmid N_0$, a Deligne–Rapoport model package $\mathfrak X$ of level $(N_0,q)$ over the subring $R = \mathbb Z_{(q)} \subset \mathbb Q$ of rationals with denominator coprime to $q$, a discrete valuation domain $O$ with a ring map $\rho_O : R \to O$ whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $q$, and an algebraically closed field $\kappa$ of characteristic $q$ with a ring map $\mathrm{toκ} : O \to \kappa$. Let $H$ be the package of site hypotheses (finiteness of the node set, existence of oriented crossing charts over the crossing quotient, the étale-neighbourhood principle, injectivity and closedness of the crossing points, and the hypotheses on the toric resolutions), and let $h\xi$ say that both marked points $\xi_0,\xi_1$ lie in the complement $X_0$ of the crossing points of the chart input $C$. Let $F^{(e)}_0,\dots,F^{(e)}_e$ be, for each $e$, ideal sheaf data on the toric resolution $\mathrm{Resolution}\,(q)\,e$, subject to the chart table: for each chart index $i : \mathrm{Fin}\,e$ and each $k$, the inverse image of $F^{(e)}_k$ along the $i$-th chart immersion $\iota$ is the ideal sheaf on $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the crossing quotient $O[X_0,X_1]/(X_0X_1 - q)$ cut out by $\langle V\rangle$ if $k = i$, by $\langle U\rangle$ if $k = i+1$, and by the unit ideal otherwise. The conclusion is that for every node $n$ (a point of the fibre product of the two components $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,0$, $\mathfrak X.\mathrm{comp}\,1$ over $\kappa$) and every $d \le w_n$, where $w_n = C.\mathrm{thick}\,n$ is the width at $n$, the component ideal sheaf $\mathrm{comp}$ at the chain position $\mathrm{chainPos}\,w\,n\,d$ — the zero component for $d = 0$, the $(d-1)$-st exceptional component of the chain over $n$ for $0 < d < w_n$, and the infinity component for $d = w_n$ — restricted to the open $\mathrm{toDR}^{-1}(U_n)$ of the glued resolution, equals the inverse image of $F^{(w_n)}_d$ along the inverse of the chart isomorphism $\mathrm{chartIso}\,n$ followed by $C.g\,n$.
--
--   This is the labelling step in the construction of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model at level $\Gamma_0(N_0q)$: it identifies, chart by chart, the components of the special fibre of the glued resolution with the canonical component family on the toric resolution of the ordinary double point $X_0X_1 = q$, so that intersection numbers and multiplicities can be read off from the toric chart table. It is cited by [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackageLevel.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageLevel_and_dRResolvedModelChartsLevelRam), which produces a `DRResolvedModelPackageLevel` together with its chart data.
